WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.419 --> 00:00:08.809
What's up, guys?

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:10.210
Jeff Cavaliere, ATHLEANX.COM.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.279
A common question that I'll get for sure is,
'Jeff.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:18.010
If you could only pick one piece of equipment
to train with, what would it be?'

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:22.550
Would it be Barbells, Dumbbells, or Cables?

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.480
My answer is, 'That's an impossible question,
guys.'

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.560
Because if you want to train and train completely,
at some point, you're likely going to want

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.770
to train with all 3.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.660
And there's one very specific reason why that
is.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.350
And that's because each one of these has its
advantages and disadvantages, and each one

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:42.089
is going to stress your body in a completely
different way.

00:00:42.089 --> 00:00:46.879
So I thought, to underscore that point I would
take one single exercise and demonstrate how

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.210
using those 3 different pieces of equipment

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.979
can drastically change the impact that exercise
has on our body.

00:00:52.979 --> 00:00:56.679
So, we'll do a Kneeling Overhead Press, ok.

00:00:56.679 --> 00:01:00.069
Again, let's get a bit of stability going
on through our core.

00:01:00.069 --> 00:01:01.670
It's a good athletic movement.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.790
We're going to get our shoulders working for
sure, but we're going to do it with 3 different

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:05.790
pieces of equipment.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:06.970
We'll start with the barbell.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:09.510
So, I've got to clean this thing up, ok.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.990
I'm talking about the advantages as soon as
I put it down.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:13.590
So, Barbell here.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:14.930
Clean it up.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.899
Get down into our lunge.

00:01:17.899 --> 00:01:19.189
Stabilize.

00:01:19.189 --> 00:01:21.759
And press.

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:24.340
And down.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:35.000
And you can see that I'm able to use, you
know, a pretty decent amount of weight with

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.000
the barbell.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.460
That's one of the big advantages of it.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:42.840
The reason why we're able to push more weight
with a barbell is because we don't have to

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:47.049
worry about the stabilizer muscles working
as hard as they do when

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:50.119
we use an individual, 3-dimensional dumbbell,
ok.

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:55.789
There's more movement ability with individual
dumbbells then there is with a fixed bar.

00:01:55.789 --> 00:02:01.439
So, that might explain why you might be able
to be a 300 pound Bench Presser, but you can't

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:03.710
press 150 pound dumbbells, alright.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.070
So, that's advantage number 1.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:09.040
A little bit heavier weight, build a little
bit more muscle.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.040
Next.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:17.549
We could go into our Dumbbell Press, and again,
come down and press up.

00:02:17.549 --> 00:02:23.819
Now, again, one of the nice things here is,
if there is an asymmetry in muscle strength

00:02:23.819 --> 00:02:24.840
from right to left,

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:30.319
it's going to be exposed here because one
arm, the one that's weaker, that was getting

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:34.040
helped by the fact that the bar was fixed
together,

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:38.420
is not going to be so lucky when you're using
dumbbells, ok.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.400
But, one of the nice things here is you're
shortening your lever arm.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:48.940
You're able to keep your dumbbells in a little
bit more, so, for this exercise, you can press

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:55.739
it without maybe that frontal plane challenge
that you had from the bar this way.

00:02:55.739 --> 00:02:59.060
because the weights were distributed a little
bit further away from you.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:03.000
So, I had to work my core a little bit more
with the barbell there as well.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.420
Again, is it an advantage or a disadvantage?

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.569
It depends on what you're trying to work.

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:09.290
If you're working for pure strength, you want
to consider that.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:14.160
Thirdly, when we use cables, you've got to
follow the line of resistance.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.970
You've got to follow the line of the cables.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:20.810
So, here, I can get down and press.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.620
And yeah, this is great.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.720
I'm still doing an Overhead Press, but guess
what's really working?

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.090
You can probably see it.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:35.689
It's my core because here I'm not just pressing
up, but the cables want to pull me back here.

00:03:35.689 --> 00:03:38.040
So I really have to work my core.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.079
So, yeah, it's a Cable Press,

00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:47.390
but we have a whole other element in play
because of the direction of the force of the

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:53.890
cables is altering definitely the direction
of force of gravity against dumbbells or a

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:54.890
barbell.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.939
So, you'll see, you've got to train everything
guys.

00:03:57.939 --> 00:04:01.700
There's really no 1 way to train if you want
a complete body.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.849
And there's no 1 exercise to train if you
want a complete body.

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:10.010
You have to put it all together, and you have
to put it together in a way that makes sense.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:14.360
I try to do that for you guys already, step-by-step
with the ATHLEANX Training Program.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:20.640
If you haven't already and you want a step-by-step
program that will layer these things in exactly

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.280
when I feel you need to start using them,

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:29.530
and also, give you guys ways around some lack
of equipment because I realize that not everybody

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.960
has access to all of this.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:36.970
I show you ways you can do it very inexpensively
with bands that cost like 10 bucks that can

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:38.050
replace these cables.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:41.960
We do that at ATHLEANX.COM in our ATHLEANX
Program.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.760
In the meantime, if you found this helpful,
make sure you leave a thumb's up and a comment

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:47.760
below.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.990
Whatever else it is that you'd like to see,
leave that in the comments, and I'll make

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.170
a video on it.

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:53.010
Alright, guys, I'll see you back here again
soon.

